From: Hummingbird maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] t: allow retries in SSH authentication HTTPS fallback tests

The invalid fallback hostname can produce a retryable DNS error in a
hermetic build. In that case the Locking and Batch API requests repeat
SSH authentication and HTTPS fallback, producing ten calls instead of
two. Require at least one fallback for each API without fixing the total
number of attempts. Keep checking that the push fails. Apply the same
allowance to the URL-encoded newline case added in git-lfs 3.8.1.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Reference: https://gitlab.com/redhat/hummingbird/rpms/-/merge_requests/4781

diff --git a/t/t-ssh.sh b/t/t-ssh.sh
--- a/t/t-ssh.sh
+++ b/t/t-ssh.sh
@@ -110,9 +110,9 @@
   if echo "$encoded_reponame" | grep -qF "%0A"; then
-    [ 2 -eq "$(grep -c "exec: lfs-ssh-echo.*git-lfs-authenticate '\\\\''/${encoded_reponame%%%0A-newline}" push.log)" ]
-    [ 2 -eq "$(grep -c "exec (cont\.): -newline'\\\\'' upload" push.log)" ]
+    [ 2 -le "$(grep -c "exec: lfs-ssh-echo.*git-lfs-authenticate '\\\\''/${encoded_reponame%%%0A-newline}" push.log)" ]
+    [ 2 -le "$(grep -c "exec (cont\.): -newline'\\\\'' upload" push.log)" ]
   else
-    [ 2 -eq "$(grep -c "exec: lfs-ssh-echo.*git-lfs-authenticate /$reponame upload" push.log)" ]
-  fi
-  [ 2 -eq "$(grep -c -F "ssh: git@$invalid_host does not provide git-lfs-authenticate, falling back to guessed LFS endpoint" push.log)" ]
-  [ 2 -eq "$(grep -c -F "HTTP: POST https://$invalid_host/$encoded_reponame/" push.log)" ]
+    [ 2 -le "$(grep -c "exec: lfs-ssh-echo.*git-lfs-authenticate /$reponame upload" push.log)" ]
+  fi
+  [ 2 -le "$(grep -c -F "ssh: git@$invalid_host does not provide git-lfs-authenticate, falling back to guessed LFS endpoint" push.log)" ]
+  [ 2 -le "$(grep -c -F "HTTP: POST https://$invalid_host/$encoded_reponame/" push.log)" ]
 }
